---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Row from '../../components/Row.astro';
import { INSTALL_PATH } from '../../data/site';

// Cursor, in the app's own words: CONNECT_WORDS.cursor, AGENTS (the setting
// by hand) and AGENT_CHECKS in crates/vault-tauri/dist/app.js. "Connect it for
// me" opens Cursor's own install link (ADR-106, ADR-SEC-031).
const snippet = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "zaaheen": {
      "command": ${JSON.stringify(INSTALL_PATH)},
      "args": ["mcp", "serve"]
    }
  }
}`;
const OUTLINE = [
  { id: 'connect', title: 'Connect it' },
  { id: 'by-hand', title: 'Add the setting yourself' },
  { id: 'check', title: 'Check it worked' },
  { id: 'using', title: 'Using it' },
];
---
<Guide
  path="/docs/connect-cursor/"
  lede="In Zaaheen, open the Agents tab, choose + Connect an AI app, then Cursor and Connect it for me. Cursor asks you to install Zaaheen: click Install, and it's connected."
  outline={OUTLINE}
>
  <section class="docs-section">
    <Row id="connect" title="Connect it" where="Agents › Connect">
      <p>Zaaheen opens Cursor's own install link, and Cursor asks you. Zaaheen never changes Cursor's
         settings itself.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>In Zaaheen, open the <em>Agents</em> tab and choose <em>+ Connect an AI app</em>.</li>
        <li>Choose <em>Cursor</em>, then <em>Connect it for me</em>.</li>
        <li>Cursor asks you to install Zaaheen. Click <em>Install</em>, and it's connected.</li>
      </ol>
    </Row>

    <Row id="by-hand" title="Add the setting yourself" where="Cursor › mcp.json">
      <p>If Zaaheen says it couldn't find or open Cursor, add the setting yourself. Add this to
         Cursor's settings file, mcp.json, in the .cursor folder in your home folder. Save it, then
         restart Cursor:</p>
      <pre><code>{snippet}</code></pre>
      <p>That is where Zaaheen usually installs. The <em>Agents</em> tab shows the setting for your
         computer exactly, ready to copy.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="check" title="Check it worked" where="Cursor › Settings">
      <p>In Cursor, open Settings, then MCP (Tools &amp; MCP in newer versions). Zaaheen has a green
         dot.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="using" title="Using it" where="Cursor">
      <p>Cursor checks Zaaheen by itself when you ask about yourself, your preferences or your work.
         What it saves there, your other connected AI apps can use too.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Guide>
